{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.pair_phase1_riccati","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.pair_phase1_riccati","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.overlap_at_small_separation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.overlap_at_small_separation","kind":"theorem","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L232-L243","doc":"**The overlap race is won before collision, `Γ`-free**: along the\n`τ`-parametrized phase-1 flow (`W(τ) = Om W₀ d₀² 1 τ`, `d²(τ) =\nd₀² − τ = x`), overlap `W ≥ x²` holds as soon as `x³ ≤ W₀·d₀²`.\nSince `W₀·d₀² > 0`, such `x > 0` exist: the cutoff engages at\npositive separation for every positive circulation history. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_hits_every_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_hits_every_level","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L177-L203","doc":"**Unboundedness on approach**: for every level `M > Ω₀` there is a\ntime `0 < t < d₀²/r` (strictly before the inviscid collision time\n`t* = d₀²/r = π d₀²/Γ`) with `Ω(t) = M`.  Phase 1 alone drives the\nenstrophy through every finite level — blow-up in the model is\nprevented only by the phase-2 overlap cutoff engaging first\n(`overlap_race_strict`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.discrete_riccati_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.discrete_riccati_lower","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L136-L175","doc":"**The pair channel satisfies the GP5 Riccati-lower-bound hypothesis\nwith uniform `c′`**: `Ω(t+δ) ≥ Ω(t) + c′·δ·Ω(t)²` for every step\n`δ ≥ 0` inside phase 1.  (From `one_div_Om_sub`,\n`Ω(t+δ) − Ω(t) = c′·δ·Ω(t)·Ω(t+δ) ≥ c′·δ·Ω(t)²` by monotonicity.)\nThis is the mechanism-level branch-A statement *during the\napproach*: while separated, the pair's enstrophy self-amplifies at\nthe exact uniform Riccati rate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_mono","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L123-L134","doc":"**Monotonicity**: `Ω(t) ≤ Ω(t+s)` whenever both times precede the\ncollision (`d² > 0` at the later time) and `r·s ≥ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_pos","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L118-L121","doc":"`Ω` is positive on the pre-collision interval. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.one_div_Om_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.one_div_Om_sub","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L106-L116","doc":"**Derivative-free uniformity of `c′`**: the reciprocal enstrophy\ndecreases at the exact constant rate `c′` —\n`1/Ω(t) − 1/Ω(t+s) = c′·s` for every `t, s`.  This is the identity\nbehind the probe's \"c′ exactly uniform in phase 1\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L76-L103","doc":"**Phase 1 is a uniform Riccati flow**: the closed form\n`Ω(t) = Ω₀ / (1 − c′·Ω₀·t)` — the exact solution of `Ω' = c′·Ω²`\nwith constant `c′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.d2_mul_Om_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.d2_mul_Om_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L69-L74","doc":"**The exact invariant**: `d²(t)·Ω(t) = d₀²·Ω₀` throughout phase 1.\n(The probe's sharp finding: `(d²Ω)' = 0`, so `c′` cannot drift.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.cPrime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.cPrime","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The uniform Riccati coefficient `c′ = r/(d₀²·Ω₀)`\n(`= Γ/(π d₀² Ω₀)`; `= 1/π` at unit parameters, the probe's value). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.Om","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L60-L62","doc":"Phase-1 enstrophy along the closed-form flow:\n`Ω(t) = Ω₀·d₀²/d²(t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.d2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PairPhase1.d2","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/pair_phase1_riccati.lean#L56-L58","doc":"Phase-1 separation-squared: `d²(t) = d₀² − r·t`, where `r = Γ/π` is\nthe constant Biot–Savart approach rate (`(d²)' = −Γ/π`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}